cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use welleng, please cite it. If you use the anti-collision
  (exact Mahalanobis separation factor) method, please also cite the
  anti-collision paper listed under references.
title: welleng
abstract: A collection of well engineering tools.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Corcutt
    given-names: Jonathan
version: 0.12.1
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jonnymaserati/welleng"
url: "https://github.com/jonnymaserati/welleng"
keywords:
  - directional drilling
  - wellbore positioning
  - anti-collision
  - ISCWSA
  - survey error model
references:
  # Gyro error-model validation paper (published).
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Reproducing the ISCWSA Gyro Error-Model Test Cases: Implementation
      Clarifications, Reference-Data Inconsistencies, and an Open-Source
      Reference Implementation
    authors:
      - family-names: Corcutt
        given-names: Jonathan
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20940515
  # Anti-collision (exact Mahalanobis separation factor) paper.
  # DOI to be added on publication; source: papers/anti-collision-conservatism.md
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Making the Exact Wellbore Anti-Collision Boundary Practical: an
      Efficient, Validated, Open Implementation, and the Cost of the
      Separation-Rule Approximation
    authors:
      - family-names: Corcutt
        given-names: Jonathan
    year: 2026
